{"title":"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Simple_Moduli)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Simple Moduli)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Confusing_But_Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Confusing But Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the sum of the digits of the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9690056fbdd20fa075dd81e71014356141eea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111111111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/1/481b9dba5499d18771af82b00d276675804095dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 18\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 27\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 45\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 63\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the standard multiplication algorithm, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/125164fccfa2010c2b1b71fedac1555eb7d7dee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111,111,111^2=12,345,678,987,654,321,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"328\" height=\"18\" /> whose digit sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df92903f798da4de27b25a23df64a500698a6a57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(E)\\text{ }81.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Simple_Moduli.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Simple_Moduli)\">Solution 2 (Simple Moduli)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Simple Moduli)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd5f9860e37971d5b5807cf289e5c656314f8de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111{,}111{,}111 \\mod 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3ccf71133e06a8203b0085c755007eb07c9e4210.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(111{,}111{,}111)^2 \\mod 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"21\" />. More importantly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> denote the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Through properties of mod9 congruences, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096c9e54569e1f6fd790d81ffa7d4c208568b984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv S(n) \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"20\" />. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/680f8b7b5feeb46a5e3c4f9e9ab1df6a7101cc12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 \\equiv (S(n))^2 \\mod 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e862919e15974611fd94c78ac017238f36b537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(111{,}111{,}111) = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"20\" />, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/f/8afea3aabb074d91862a1af98ed49774a003e2b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^2 = \\boxed{081}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"81\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/312d643c239f9fd6054701a8cba664779329cf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf307af5793b1820789a10c54f8240188778f66e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11^2 = 121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4145a06985618b682a498fde6af02c947dfcab7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111^2 = 12321$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />,\n</p><p>and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c1514d30add3c8e58d6ab22f7969aa5cb0f7d3fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,111^2 = 1234321$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can clearly see the pattern: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aa75d393c0018241cc8ef2574769737b66fb608.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111\\cdots111$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"12\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> ones (and for the sake of simplicity, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e6f0c3c9d936a99e222471be73bb8fa3d243c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&lt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />), then the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0872ca2f62e98f7846c7ed24f6953417c2643dbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X^2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"15\" /> is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e8115162b14832def838dbbcc63b6ace0c948d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+5\\cdots n+(n-1)+(n-2)\\cdots+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55022cc68c5d34ca1609e91c3da60cf404b87ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=(1+2+3\\cdots n)+(1+2+3+\\cdots n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"338\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b4deaad0b3cfe001c389df2592b1edbe0c46cd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\dfrac{n(n+1)}{2}+\\dfrac{(n-1)n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"182\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf71e6f7ee0bd804521d07afbe025e700df6ac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\dfrac{n(n+1+n-1)}{2}=\\dfrac{2n^2}{2}=n^2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"256\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Aha! We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/7/2975b7bd780b46cc9e02a61f6ebe1e7dcaf1a359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111,111,111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"17\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits, so its digit sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/394776726077dd525a71d6a142dbd047df3b12a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^2=\\boxed{81(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fb15e35c9dcd641c347a238e30c0cc36bfddfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/9190dd3baff01f4a8937710477560759d6d98086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111(100+10+1)=11100+1110+111=12321$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"386\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can apply this strategy to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/7/ac79334a384b49b5a03ae275072ce5121160c4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111,111,111^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />, as seen below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/5/765ee723c0a0e7ca3c1a1a83383d73125019ef53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111111111^2=111111111(100000000+10000000\\cdots+10+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"480\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843ee4e8332fd7146c15b6fd325aa3af280e91e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=11111111100000000+1111111110000000+\\cdots+111111111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"491\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fcb794e0680e364409619be15e1193ae8b774e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=12,345,678,987,654,321$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"213\" height=\"16\" /> \n</p><p>The digit sum is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/3824608674a44bc5e7a96f73c7d83dbd45368c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9+8+7+6+5+4+3+2+1=81 \\boxed{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"592\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Confusing_But_Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Confusing_But_Fast)\">Solution 5 (Confusing But Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Confusing But Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that the only way for the sum of multiple numbers' digits to not equal the sum of the digits after they are all added is for a place (i.e., tens place, ones place, etc.) to be carried over. If that was a little confusing, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/7/2b7d1484f6fd6dddbecdbe7422ac85b98f19cd7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63+22=85,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/1/2211afadb47bebfc1ff6f0adc4eaefa1723480ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+5=13.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f96245c7d53e44a217a24c709407a91669e555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+3+2+2=13,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" /> too. The ones don't carry over to the tens and the tens don't carry over to the hundreds. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8efe7d988d3364285a48889c1c4748ebb706a064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63+37=100,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ef129032aae8f3a0dfb9de5c3cae42b6115196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+3+3+7=19 \\neq 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" /> The ones carry over to the tens and the tens carry over to the hundreds, meaning it loses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/19649e64ad7c632503f134c329562a8f0ce2c24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(9-1)=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> of its digit sum.\n</p><p><br />\nIf that made sense, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd9690056fbdd20fa075dd81e71014356141eea2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$111111111$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> digits. Since the only operation in long multiplication will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/c/92c5770c5ac85900b35548289121eda8fbab3ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and the addition tower will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> stacks long, there is no way a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> stack can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> long and carry over its value. Thus, it is sufficient to conclude that we will multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e489326ba6f5e8498912742642b0042bf939e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 9= \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"121\" height=\"30\" /> times, with no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> being carried over.\n</p><p>~ Wesserwes7254\n</p><p>Note to author: This made sense <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/325584771876788668592b6e6a783c6b201013de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$:)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that for the patterns,\n\\begin{aligned}\n&amp; 1^2=1 \\\\\n&amp; 11^2=121 \\\\\n&amp; 111^2=12321 \\\\\n&amp; \\text{So} , (11111111)^2=12345678987654321\n\\end{aligned}\n</p><p>natural numbers from 1 to go up then down, and number of 1 's gives the middle number \nfor this arrangement and obviously this tricks applicable for number of 1,s <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970c8ae0aa25198a21553ab59afb2c30be2894cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> .\nSum of digits, \n\\( 1+2+3+\\cdots+8+9+8+\\cdots+3+2+1 \\) \\( =9^2=81 \\) (Square of the middle number)\n</p><p>~KENJAKURA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A\">2009 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"20